# Keeps the deploy payload to what the site actually needs.
# Without this the upload was 72MB and timed out mid-transfer; ~46MB of that
# was working material that is never served — screenshots, PDFs, print assets.
#
# Deploy-time only — this does not affect git, and everything listed still runs
# locally. Everything here is working material that is never served.
#
# There is no longer a "routes kept off the public site" section. Those routes
# (/studios, /truck, /clahvay, /ai and every /explore variant) were deleted
# outright on 2026-09-03 — see DECISIONS.md. Hiding a route at deploy time while
# it still built locally meant the repo and the live site disagreed about what
# the product was; deleting them settles it in one place. Their prices and copy
# are transcribed in docs/salvage-2026-09-03.md.

# Reference screenshots + design captures
explore-shots/
IMG_*.png
IMG_*.jpg

# Print + sales collateral
business-card/
pitch/
info.pdf
*.pdf

# Working docs and notes
docs/
NOTES.md
DEPLOY.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
DECISIONS.md
CLAUDE-BUILD-ORDER.md
foundos-brand-and-site-spec.md
foundos-system-rulebook.md

# Tooling state
.serena/
.claude/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Build-time tooling. scripts/capture-work.mjs regenerates the concept-site
# screenshots in public/work/ — it runs on a machine, never on the server, and
# the images it produces ARE deployed.
scripts/

# ── Never serve these ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under public/ is served verbatim whether or not a page links to it.
# Nothing referenced these, which is exactly why nobody noticed they were live.
#
# public/portfolio/ held 18 screenshots reachable at foundos.ai/portfolio/*.png,
# among them heirloom.png, clahvay.png, amistad.png, babygirl.png and
# station11.png — five real businesses that have never hired us. src/lib/contact.ts
# already names those exact businesses and says why: showing them reads as
# "client" to a visitor, which is untrue, and it risks a live deal if an owner
# ever finds their restaurant used as someone else's portfolio piece. A direct
# URL does that just as effectively as a link on a page.
#
# public/josh.jpg is a 320px photo from a music night with another woman's face
# centred in it and more people behind. She never agreed to appear on a business
# website. It is not used anywhere and must not be served.
#
# Keeping them here rather than deleting them: they are useful working material
# for pitches. They are just not the public's business.
public/portfolio/
public/josh.jpg

# Deployed from its own Vercel project (istanbul-demo-sigma) — not from here.
src/app/demo/istanbul/
public/demo/istanbul/
